.TH DROIDIAN-APEX 8 "August 2026" "droidian-apex 1.0.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
droidian-apex \- manage Android APEX modules for Droidian
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B droidian-apex
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B droidian-apex
discovers Android Pony EXpress modules before apexd starts, mounts flattened or
packaged modules, and mirrors apexd's live mounts from a Halium LXC container to
the Droidian host.
.PP
Discovery does not require the container to be running. By default the program
searches APEX directories below
.IR /android/system ,
.IR /android/system_ext ,
.IR /android/product ,
.IR /android/vendor ,
.IR /android/odm ,
and
.IR /android/data/apex/active .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-android-root =PATH
Use PATH as the root containing Android partitions. The default is
.BR /android .
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mount-root =PATH
Use PATH for host APEX mounts. The default is
.BR /apex .
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-container =NAME
Use the named LXC container. The default is
.BR android .
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timeout =SECONDS
Set the apexd wait timeout. The default is 60 seconds.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry-run
Inspect packages and print mount operations without changing mounts.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print discovery, container, and property state transitions.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the program version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR list " [" \-\-json "] [" ROOT " ...]"
Enumerate flattened directories, packaged APEXs, and compressed APEXs. Explicit
roots may be an APEX source directory, a directory containing APEXs, or an APEX
file. This command never contacts apexd.
.TP
.BR mount " [" \-\-all " | " PATH " ...]"
Mount the highest version of each module. Flattened modules use read-only bind
mounts. Packaged modules use read-only loop mounts, with automatic ext4/EROFS
detection. Compressed APEXs are unpacked transiently. This command requires
root unless
.B \-\-dry-run
is used.
.TP
.B prepare
Alias for
.BR "mount --all" .
.TP
.BR wait " [started|activated|ready]"
Wait for the container and the requested apexd property state. Later states
satisfy waits for earlier states. The default is
.BR ready .
.TP
.B status
Print LXC state, init PID, and the value of
.BR apexd.status .
.TP
.B sync
Wait for apexd to become ready, locate the container mount namespace through
.IR /proc/PID/root/apex ,
and read-only bind the canonical module paths to the host APEX root. This is the
preferred command for lxc-android startup integration.
.TP
.BR apexd " status"
Show container and apexd state.
.TP
.BR apexd " wait [STATE]"
Wait for apexd. Equivalent to the top-level
.B wait
command.
.TP
.BR apexd " dump [ARG ...]"
Run
.B dumpsys apexservice
inside the container. If its active-package section is empty, append a package
list derived from the container's live
.B /apex
mounts. Any additional dumpsys arguments are passed through unchanged and
disable this fallback.
.TP
.B diagnose
Report configuration, required device nodes and filesystems, mount state, LXC
state, apexd status, and every pre-start APEX candidate.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DROIDIAN_APEX_ANDROID_ROOT
Default Android partition root.
.TP
.B DROIDIAN_APEX_MOUNT_ROOT
Default host APEX mount root.
.TP
.B DROIDIAN_APEX_CONTAINER
Default LXC container name.
.TP
.B DROIDIAN_APEX_TIMEOUT
Default wait timeout in seconds.
.SH SECURITY
The direct
.B mount
command parses and mounts payloads but does not implement apexd signature or
dm-verity verification. Use it only with trusted APEXs from Android's verified,
read-only partitions. For the normal boot path, use
.BR sync ,
which mirrors mounts already activated and verified by apexd.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success, one indicates an operational failure or timeout, and
two indicates invalid command-line usage.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /usr/sbin/droidian-apex
Program executable.
.TP
.B /run/droidian-apex-manager
Short-lived extraction files used while mounting compressed payloads.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lxc-attach (1),
.BR lxc-info (1),
.BR mount (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Erik Inkinen <erik.inkinen@erikinkinen.fi>
